{#
  module/Schoenstatt/view/schoenstatt/admin/index.phtml, ported.

  Both are live until SYMFONY_KERNEL is set in production: this one renders under the
  Symfony front controller, the .phtml under the laminas one. See docs/strangler.md.

  Three notes on the translation from thirteen lines of .phtml:

  - **The per-item ACL check is the page**, not decoration. `route/admin` admits
    sch_moderator and translator; a translator then sees one of these ten links.
    Dropping the check would show every moderator tool to a translator, which is why
    it is here and not in the controller — same place the original has it.
  - **`badge()` is reproduced rather than reached.** TwbBundle's helper renders
    `<span class="badge">N</span>` and the original disables its translator, so the
    markup is a literal here. Reaching a laminas form-view helper for one span would
    add it to App\Laminas\ViewHelpers' allowlist for no gain.
  - **The whitespace is not reproduced.** The .phtml emits nine spaces between `</a>`
    and `</p>` — an artifact of where its `?>` tags fall. Ten lines is few enough
    that a real difference cannot hide in the noise, so the two renderings are
    compared by content (the ordered href/label/badge triples, pinned in
    test/Smoke/AdminAuthorizationSmokeTest) rather than by bytes.
#}
{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{% block content %}
{% for route, text in pages %}
    {%- if is_allowed('route/' ~ route) %}
<p><a href="{{ laminas_path(route) }}">{{ translate(text) }}</a>{% if badges[route] is defined %} <span class="badge">{{ badges[route] }}</span>{% endif %}</p>
    {%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{% endblock %}
